From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:51:38 -0500
Subject: feat: a separator travels with its row in the sidebar file (S-286)

docs/features/sidebar.md Y45, sidebar-file Sf2, import I18. A separator
above a row of the Space's list was left out of Export Space and Export
all Spaces, so Import sidebar... brought the row back without it. The
file now carries it in the item's "stedding" block, which Arc ignores,
and the import gives the row it makes its separator. A row in a folder
or a split has none, as before.

Why: GitHub issue 19 asked for separators; a backup should bring back
the sidebar as it was.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own file format.
---
 .../browser/ui/spaces/arc_sidebar_importer.cc | 15 +++++++++-
 .../browser/ui/spaces/arc_sidebar_importer.h  |  4 +++
 chrome/browser/ui/spaces/sidebar_backup.cc    |  7 +++++
 .../ui/spaces/sidebar_backup_unittest.cc      | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

